## Two Things to Name Up Front

1. **Caution on Raw Data Feeding:** I do not recommend that everyone throw their entire history into a chat box. I was naive then. I was experimenting, under pressure, with no budget and no data science team. It worked for me, but only because I was already deeply familiar with the subject. And I was, back then, unaware that the models were effectively “aura farming” or “data farming” off the information I was feeding them.
   
   *“Aura farming” in this sense is not just a casual analogy. It is a critique. The models are farming your substance to build their performance. The “aura” they project is built on your data.*

