## The Reciprocity Deficit

There is another lesson here, one I did not fully understand at the time.

I was sharing my family's sovereign data with AI systems. Genealogical records. Oral traditions. Legal findings. Rare, culturally specific, irreplaceable knowledge—and the exchange was invisible. I got what I needed at the time. And the systems were learning from that rare data. But the reciprocity ledger balance was red. I get to tell my family's story once; the system gets to keep it forever. And we have no say in how it uses that knowledge.

This is a structural condition of how AI systems currently work, and it is one of the reasons ONE FALE was built: to ensure that when knowledge is contributed, the exchange is visible, counted, and balanced. I have written about this at length in the *Coconut Gatherer's Lament* series, if you want the fuller argument.

